            <ArticleTitle>Pain modulation and the action of analgesic medications.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S42-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A general approach to improving the treatment of patients with post-herpetic neuralgia is outlined. Pain-generating processes initiated by injury to peripheral nerve and new treatments that target these processes are discussed. Another described approach is to use knowledge of central nervous system pain-modulating networks to improve the effectiveness of centrally acting analgesics such as opioids and tricyclic antidepressants.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
